# ALX Practical 1

## Objective

This practical focused on setting up a cybersecurity lab environment and becoming familiar with Linux navigation, SSH, SCP, and port forwarding.

## Skills Practiced

- Oracle VirtualBox
- Kali Linux
- SSH
- SCP
- Linux Commands
- File Management
- Port Forwarding

## What I Learned

- How to set up a virtual lab safely.
- Basic Linux terminal navigation.
- Secure remote access using SSH.
- File transfer using SCP.
- Different SSH tunneling techniques.

## Challenges

The practical required careful attention to Linux commands and understanding how SSH works in different scenarios.

## Key Takeaways

Building a personal lab environment is essential for practicing cybersecurity skills safely and effectively.